1018:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** /** @defgroup UART_Exported_Functions_Group2 IO operation functions
1019:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****   * @brief UART Transmit/Receive functions
1020:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****   *
1021:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** @verbatim
1022:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****  ===============================================================================
1023:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****                       ##### IO operation functions #####
1024:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****  ===============================================================================
1025:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the UART asynchronous
1026:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     and Half duplex data transfers.
1027:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1028:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
1029:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The communication is performed in polling mode.
1030:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL status of all data processing is returned by the same function
1031:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            after finishing transfer.
1032:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The communication is performed using Interrupts
1033:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            or DMA, These API's return the HAL status.
1034:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1035:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
1036:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            using DMA mode.
1037:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback() user callbacks
1038:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            will be executed respectively at the end of the transmit or Receive process
1039:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a communication error is
1040:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1041:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Blocking mode API's are :
1042:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Transmit()
1043:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Receive()
1044:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1045:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API's with Interrupt are :
1046:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Transmit_IT()
1047:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Receive_IT()
1048:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_IRQHandler()
1049:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1050:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API's with DMA are :
1051:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Transmit_DMA()
1052:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Receive_DMA()
1053:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_DMAPause()
1054:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_DMAResume()
1055:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_DMAStop()
1056:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1057:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) A set of Transfer Complete Callbacks are provided in Non_Blocking mode:
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccrZx1zi.s 			page 20


1058:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_TxHalfCpltCallback()
1059:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback()
1060:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_RxHalfCpltCallback()
1061:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback()
1062:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()
1063:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1064:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode transfers could be aborted using Abort API's :
1065:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Abort()
1066:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortTransmit()
1067:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortReceive()
1068:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_Abort_IT()
1069:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortTransmit_IT()
1070:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortReceive_IT()
1071:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1072:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For Abort services based on interrupts (HAL_UART_Abortxxx_IT), a set of Abort Complete Call
1073:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortCpltCallback()
1074:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortTransmitCpltCallback()
1075:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UART_AbortReceiveCpltCallback()
1076:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1077:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) A Rx Event Reception Callback (Rx event notification) is available for Non_Blocking modes o
1078:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         reception services:
1079:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback()
1080:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1081:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Wakeup from Stop mode Callback:
1082:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_WakeupCallback()
1083:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1084:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) In Non-Blocking mode transfers, possible errors are split into 2 categories.
1085:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         Errors are handled as follows :
1086:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Error is considered as Recoverable and non blocking : Transfer could go till end, but er
1087:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            to be evaluated by user : this concerns Frame Error, Parity Error or Noise Error
1088:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            in Interrupt mode reception .
1089:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            Received character is then retrieved and stored in Rx buffer, Error code is set to allow
1090:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback() user callback is executed.
1091:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            Transfer is kept ongoing on UART side.
1092:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            If user wants to abort it, Abort services should be called by user.
1093:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Error is considered as Blocking : Transfer could not be completed properly and is aborte
1094:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            This concerns Overrun Error In Interrupt mode reception and all errors in DMA mode.
1095:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            Error code is set to allow user to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()
1096:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****            user callback is executed.
1097:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1098:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****     -@- In the Half duplex communication, it is forbidden to run the transmit
1099:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c ****         and receive process in parallel, the UART state HAL_UART_STATE_BUSY_TX_RX can't be useful.
1100:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1101:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_uart.c **** @endverbatim
